<article class="env-proposition" id="0GA3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GA3">Proposition <span data-tag="0GA3">51.21.7</span>.</a> Let $I$ be an ideal of a Noetherian ring $A$. Let $t \geq 0$ be an upper bound on the number of generators of $I$. There exist $N, c \geq 0$ such that for $n \geq N$ the maps </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  A/I^ n \to A/I^{n - c}  \]
</div>
  <p> satisfy the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0G9V" data-tag="0G9V">51.20.2</a> with $e = t$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate consequence of Lemmas <a href="/tag/0GA2" data-tag="0GA2">51.21.6</a> and <a href="/tag/0G9V" data-tag="0G9V">51.20.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>